princess charlene of monaco is  temporarily stepping down from official  duties while she seeks treatment in a  facility just outside the country in a  new interview with people her husband  prince albert ii of monaco reveals that  the 43 year old princess is suffering  profound quote exhaustion both emotional  and physical the decision to seek  medical care comes just days after her  return home to monaco the princess  previously spent six months in south  africa due to an ear nose and throat  infection which involved a number of  corrective surgeries resulting in an  extended stay we are finally back it's  been a while one week after sharing a  photo of her happy reunion with husband  albert and their six-year-old twins  charlene announced she was pulling out  of monaco's national day festivities on  november 19th citing profound general  fatigue with ongoing rumors that the  couple is going through marriage  troubles prince albert clarifies quote  this has nothing to do with our  relationship i want to make that clear  it's of a different nature he goes on to  say that her current state is the result  of several factors which are private  matters adding quote she was clearly  exhausted physically and emotionally she  was overwhelmed and couldn't face  official duties life in general or even  family life  the prince also dispels rumors that  charlene's treatment is for covid or  cancer he also shuts down speculation of  plastic surgery albert adds that  charlene agreed to seek treatment after  he conducted an intervention with her  brothers and sister-in-law noting that  she had already made her decision and  that they only wanted her to confirm it  in front of them quote she wanted this  she already knew the best thing to do  was to go and have a rest and have a  real medically framed treatment as for  how the family will handle the  separation well albert is looking for  love and support from those around him  including the people of monaco
 

